&lt;p&gt;# Comments: 0&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50025601</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 19:34:45 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Show HN: Lacuna – open-source inline AI writing suggestions for your Mac</title><link>https://jackdamon.org/blog/lacuna/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;This past week I built (prompted) a tool I find myself using day to day and wanted to share it with others who may find it useful as well.&lt;p&gt;“Lacuna” is an opinionated way to invoke LLMs into any text input on your Mac. Specifically, you can type bracketed phrases {such as this}, press Shift-Command-K (or a different shortcut of your choosing), and the tool sends your bracketed phrase + the surrounding text contents to an LLM of your configuration for generating text to replace the bracketed phrase. The program returns 3 candidate phrases and the experience is entirely keyboard navigable.&lt;p&gt;Demo: &lt;a href="https://jackdamon.org/assets/images/lacuna-scheduling-demo.gif" rel="nofollow"&gt;https://jackdamon.org/assets/images/lacuna-scheduling-demo.g...&lt;/a&gt;&lt;p&gt;Example scheduling workflow using Lacuna’s native UI and sample suggestions.&lt;p&gt;So far I find myself frequently using it when drafting emails where I want help with quick phrasing.&lt;p&gt;The project was inspired by Rectangle, an open source utility app for window tiling that is keyboard based.&lt;p&gt;Lacuna is open source and available here: &lt;a href="https://github.com/jdamon96/lacuna" rel="nofollow"&gt;https://github.com/jdamon96/lacuna&lt;/a&gt;&lt;p&gt;Blog: &lt;a href="https://jackdamon.org/blog/lacuna/" rel="nofollow"&gt;https://jackdamon.org/blog/lacuna/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
